I come back to my building.
I see my neighbor, Asha, near the lift.
Her dog, Moti, is with her.
Moti sees me.
He wags his tail.
"Namaste Maya, how are you?" Asha asks.
"Namaste Asha, I am absolutely fine," I say.
"The evening weather is very nice today," I say.
"Yes, the wind is very cool," Asha says.
Moti sniffs my shoes.
He jumps with joy.
"Moti is very energetic today," I laugh.
"Yes, he wants to play outside," Asha says.
"What are you making for dinner?" Asha asks.
"I am making dal and rice today," I answer.
"Very good, I am making paneer," Asha says.
We talk for a little while longer.
Asha goes outside with Moti.
I go inside my flat.
Mumbai feels like my home now.
